        <h2>Summary / Description</h2>
        <div class="description">
          OBJECTIVES: <BR>
•	Determination of the new thermo-physiological properties of new fabrics under different environmental conditions including 1-g and micro-g conditions<br>
•	Determination of thermo-physiological parameters of the new fabrics using the Hohenstein Skin Model;  evaluation of water vapor resistance (breathability), thermal resistance (heat insulation), buffering of vaporous and liquid sweat, liquid sweat transport and drying time, thermal insulation in wet state. <br>
•	Determination of the skin sensorial comfort of the textiles: Wet cling index, number of contact points, bending stiffness, sorption index, surface index.

<P>
APPROACH: <br>
The crewmember should wear the SpaceTex Garments during regular cardiovascular work-out sessions of 45-75 minutes in duration, with a minimum intensity of 50% VO2 max or higher for at least 15 minutes. Two garments will be used, and each garment is worn during two exercise sessions (total of four preflight and four postflight sessions).  After the exercises, the crewmember will be asked to fill out a short questionnaire that asks about wear comfort etc.  After the second BDC session, each garment will be stowed inside a ziplock bag with a Tenax tube and returned to the Hohenstein Institute for microbiological analysis within three months.
<p>
Astronauts shall be equipped with a set of clothes fabricated from the latest new fabrics developed by the Schoeller AG (SPACETEX).  They shall wear those garments during regular exercise sessions.  It is up to the astronaut preference to choose either short or long versions of clothing made from one fabric. If the long garment is chosen, then the short garment must be worn underneath because short and long garments are engineered to perfectly interact as a system regarding sweat and moisture management. Each fabric shall be worn at least twice.
<p>
At a minimum four inflight sessions are required (two for each fabric).  The crewmember shall put on the top and pants, and wear the garment during exercises SpaceTex work-out sessions should be at least 45 minutes in duration, but no longer than 75 minutes.  For a minimum of 15 minutes the workout intensity should be above 50% VO2 max.  The performed exercises should be very similar during all testing sessions (exercise type and intensity), exercises sessions performed on CEVIS and/or COLBERT are preferred.  Information about the measured preflight VO2 max and the exact workout profile performed (together with HR and other supporting data as available) will be requested via data sharing from Space Medicine.  The workout intensity should not exceed 75% VO2 max anytime during the session.  After exercising, the crewmember shall fill out a short questionnaire.
<p>
Each Garment is worn twice and then shall be packed in a sealed bag together with a Tenax tube and returned to Earth for microbiological analysis within three months.

<P>
RESULTS:  <br>
Results for this experiment are currently not available.
<end>
